{"kind":"assert","text":"C3 ruling on 87a9a9a0, the construction ports.\n\nAccepted as you propose:\n- The clock port `{ now, set, clear }`, with the wall clock as the\n  default. One timer owns the send deadlines and the schedule.\n- `drafts` as a read port by key. C4 owns slots and each change.\n- `request(client, key, kind, values)` in a source module that\n  `scope.ts` does not export. Tests and C4 import it directly.\n- `scope.ts` exports `scopeClient`, the types of the view and the\n  pure status function. It exports no submit until C4.\n\nChanged: the identity. Each fact enters the options one time. Your\nproposal gives the key three times (`signer`, `actor`, and the\ncontext of `observe`) and the membership two times, and an author\ncan give values that disagree.\n- The options take `signer` and one value `member`, which holds the\n  service, the membership, the member and the principal.\n- The client derives the `PredictionActor` from `signer.key` and\n  `member`. It derives the custody `Identity` from `member`,\n  `signer.key` and the handle. The options hold no `actor`.\n- If `packages/client` already has a type that holds these facts\n  after a join, use that type for `member` and name it in the C3\n  note.\n- `observe` stays a port, as in C2, because the tests need it. Its\n  context repeats the membership, the member and the key. C4 carries\n  the remedy: the constructor that a page calls takes one value and\n  builds `signer`, `member` and `observe` from it. Write that duty\n  in the C3 note under \"Carried to C4\".\n\nNo kernel export and no wire shape: confirmed as the condition.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}